-q
----------------------------------------------------------------------
10 CLS
20 B% = 3
30 C% = 5
40 D% = 6
50 E% = 0
60 F% = -1
' XOR truth table, on variables so that nothing is folded
70 A% = E% XOR E%
75 PRINT "0", A%
80 A% = E% XOR F%
85 PRINT "-1", A%
90 A% = F% XOR E%
95 PRINT "-1", A%
100 A% = F% XOR F%
105 PRINT "0", A%
' XOR works bit by bit, it is not a boolean operation
110 A% = 3 XOR 5
115 PRINT "6", A%
120 A% = B% XOR C%
125 PRINT "6", A%
130 A% = 3 XOR C%
135 PRINT "6", A%
140 A% = B% XOR 5
145 PRINT "6", A%
' Priorities: XOR is less priority than AND and OR
150 A% = B% XOR C% AND D%
155 PRINT "7", A%
160 A% = B% XOR C% OR D%
165 PRINT "4", A%
' Special cases with a constant operand: reduced by the compiler with a warning
170 A% = 0 XOR B%
175 PRINT "3", A%
180 A% = B% XOR 0
185 PRINT "3", A%
190 A% = -1 XOR B%
195 PRINT "-4", A%
200 A% = B% XOR -1
205 PRINT "-4", A%
----------------------------------------------------------------------
WARNING: at 31:12 line 170 - XOR operation with 0 reduced to no operation; consider to remove the useless XOR
WARNING: at 33:13 line 180 - XOR operation with 0 reduced to no operation; consider to remove the useless XOR
WARNING: at 35:13 line 190 - XOR operation with -1 reduced to inversion; consider to replace XOR with NOT
WARNING: at 37:13 line 200 - XOR operation with -1 reduced to inversion; consider to replace XOR with NOT
